  "construction": "Calibration at exactly the neighbour exposure the 120 permanently-unsampled LGAs face. The 200 held-out LGAs are T16's, read from data/derived/calibration_matched.csv and not redrawn; only the partition is new.  For a group of 40, unobserved neighbour-ends are sum of a_i (queen neighbours among the permanent 120) plus twice the edges of the 200 whose both ends fall inside that group.  The first term sums to A = 146 over the 200 and is fixed; the second sums to 2*S_E, which the partition chooses: an edge between two held-out LGAs in different groups is observed by both fits.  Five groups at 0.95 require A + 2*S_E = 190, so S_E = 22: about 178 of the 200 edges among the 200 must be cut across groups, i.e. 4-5 inside each group of 40 against T16's 94.  The partition was found by a greedy conflict-minimising start plus a deterministic swap search on sum_g (total_g - 38)^2 with exactly 40 per group, seed 20261124.  Each group is one fit: that group's households are dropped and the identical household-level binomial model refitted (ten design columns of eight covariates, BYM2 on the 774-node queen graph built from the ADM2 polygons, IID cluster effect, INLA 25.10.19 defaults, no area-level covariates), then all 774 LGAs predicted from prediction rows at each LGA's mean covariate profile taken from the FULL household file (covariates held known), cluster effect marginalised by the same 7-point Gauss-Hermite rule as scripts/lga_model.R.  The truth is the direct unweighted proportion from each held-out LGA's own households, cluster-robust ratio linearisation (strata = state, PSU = cluster) with median-design-effect imputation for single-cluster LGAs. z = (model_mean - direct)/sqrt(model_var + design_var).  Pass rule fixed before any fit and identical to T12, T13 and T16: mean(z) in [-0.15,0.15], sd(z) in [0.85,1.15], share |z| <= 1.96 in [0.90,0.98].  Cluster counts and the observed/unobserved split come from data/derived/cluster_lga_fixed.csv and are cross-checked against the household file. Count-functional calibration is NOT tested: it needs joint draws per fold.",
